# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, so a file can
# differ between two clones of the same commit. That matters here for two files in
# particular: the shell scripts and YAML read by a POSIX tool, and play.ps1, which
# Windows PowerShell parses (it is ASCII-only precisely so that parsing is
# predictable).
#
# `text=auto` normalises text files to LF in the repository and lets each platform
# check them out in its native form.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch and PowerShell files are happier with CRLF on disk.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touch these.
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
